  "full_text": "They're gonna export ham to the Muslim countries in a talk restaurant. They got a picture of the Virgin Mary on the wall. They're probably not the owners. So I asked them if they wanted me to advertise. Not them, but the girl who was in there earlier. Said, no, don't advertise. So it's like, I guess what you want is just enough money to get by. And then you can sit around and talk to your wife all day. So like, the worst thing is a schedule. I can't handle a fucking schedule. I've had no schedule, no... No schedule for like 20 years. It drives me bonkers if I have an appointment. It's like for like two days, it's like, oh my God, am I going to be awake or asleep or what? What if I'm tired at that time? So the worst, I cannot handle a schedule. Immediately it would be hell. If I'm on a schedule, it's absolute hell. Like if you tell me I have to, I can only sleep from 12 to 8. If I had to do something every day at a certain time. It ruins everything. Like, I'm all fucked up. It's like, oh my God, oh my God, am I going to be awake? I told a joke about sending ham to Muslim countries. Gary Davis, I'm the smartest programmer that's ever lived. I was chosen by God to make his temple, and I was given divine power. So you actually fucked up the song, and then you make people think that my dancing is fake. So it's actually kind of not really appreciated, but I guess so. You fucked up the song. You took out, you changed the best,",
